        "name": "tag-extension-invalid-reserved-tag",
        "description": "A structural reserved tag is extended with a term (Onset/Blah, Event-context/Blah). Reserved tags must not be extended although they inherit extensionAllowed from Property. A # after a reserved tag (Onset/#) is tested in tag-extension-invalid-reserved-tag-placeholder, since it may be reported under either of two codes.",
        "warning": false,
        "schema": "8.4.0",
        "error_category": "semantic",
        "common_causes": [
            "Adding a descriptive word after Onset or Event-context as if it were a label",
            "Assuming every tag under Property may be extended because the schema browser shows extensionAllowed"
        ],
        "explanation": "Reserved tags such as Onset, Offset, Inset, Event-context, and Definition have a fixed meaning that tools rely on, so they must not be extended, even though they sit under Property, which allows extensions. A word after the tag (Onset/Blah) is an extension. Describe the event in the group's inner group or anchor definition instead.",
        "correction_strategy": "Remove the extension from the reserved tag and put the information in an ordinary tag inside the group",
        "correction_examples": [
            {
                "wrong": "(Onset/Blah, Def/MyColor)",
                "correct": "(Onset, Def/MyColor, (Label/Blah))",
                "explanation": "The extra word moves into an inner group as a Label"
            },
            {
                "wrong": "(Event-context/Blah, (Red))",
                "correct": "(Event-context, (Red))",
                "explanation": "Event-context takes no extension"
            }
        ],
